 "relevance_note": "One of the 7 transplanted patients has LAD-I with a described CD18 variant: \"Patient 5 (LAD1) had a 2490 base pair deletion\".",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; a script only assembled the JSON. The paper is a 7-patient SCT series for PIDs; only patient 5 (LAD1) is in scope; the other 6 (HIgM, SCID, CGD, WAS) get no rows. Tables 1-4 (clinical features, graft/conditioning, engraftment, chimerism) appear only as titles in the Markdown, with no content, so per-patient ages, donor details and Table 1 clinical features could not be extracted. Label 'patient 5' is the form used most often (twice lowercase, once capitalised). Gene printed as 'CD18' (no ITGB2 symbol). Variant type 'large deletion/CNV' is mapped from the stated '2490 base pair deletion'; zygosity, inheritance and parental testing are not stated. Post-SCT complications (ARDS, Pseudomonas pneumonia, E. coli sepsis, renal impairment, GI bleed, graft failure) are recorded as observed with onset 'Post-SCT'; the checklist items lower respiratory tract infection and sepsis are marked observed from these post-transplant events. Pre-SCT 'multiple infections' are unspecified, so no checklist item was set from them. 'Poor nutritional state' was not mapped to failure to thrive. Cause of death is not stated explicitly, so it is 'not reported'. Conditioning taken from the named-group statement 'Except for patient 3, busulfan was used in all regimens...'. Group counts (pulmonary infections in 4 of 7, 1 patient with GVHD) were not attributed. No contradictions found.",
